  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Post-processor",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Post-processor\"**\n\nThe site is a post-processor's result window. The ground is graphite, the ink is near-white, and the only saturated colour is the viridis colour map that Zephyr's own solutions are coloured with: the data's colour bar, from which the single accent, a viridis teal-green, is drawn for links and the reader's current place. Dark is the default (`colorMode.defaultMode: \"dark\"`, `respectPrefersColorScheme: false`); light is the variant, the same structure on a cool white ground, offered by the navbar switch.\n\nThe start page opens on one result: the uCRM transport wing, panelled and solved by Zephyr, filling a dark viewport with the offer laid over it, then three capabilities each shown by real output, then one listing. Doc pages keep the standard Docusaurus structure (rail, page, on-page contents) in the same palette. Density is a reference tool's: compact chrome, quiet 1px cool borders, prose held to a reading measure, and figures, tables and code allowed full width.\n\nDepth comes from tone, not shadow. Surfaces step from ground to surface to raised; nothing glows. Motion is a 150ms colour or border change, plus one resolve on the start page where the solution fades in over its own panel mesh.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Graphite ground, near-white ink, viridis as the one saturated family.",
      "One accent, a viridis teal-green, for links, active rail entries, focus rings and the caret.",
      "Host Grotesk for text and headings; Red Hat Mono for code and numeric readouts.",
      "Small radii (4 to 12px), 1px cool borders, flat surfaces.",
      "Every image is the library's own output, rendered from a solved case.",
      "The start page's result window is dark in both themes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colour Bar Rule",
        "body": "Outside code listings and the caution border, the only saturated colour on any page is viridis: the map itself on data, and the one teal accent drawn from it. A new hue needs a data reason.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Result Window Rule",
        "body": "The start page's hero and the three capability visuals are dark in both themes. Their renders carry pale wake lines and viridis polygons on a transparent ground that only read on graphite, so the hero pins its own palette (`--h-ground`, `--h-ink`, and so on, equal to the dark tokens) and the navbar over it is forced to dark ink. Everything outside those frames follows the theme.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readout Rule",
        "body": "Red Hat Mono is for code and for numbers a solver produced. It is never a label face or a decorative voice.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tight Display Rule",
        "body": "Tracking tightens as size grows: -0.035em at display, -0.03em at headline, -0.02em at h2, -0.01em at h3, none in body.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Glow Rule",
        "body": "Nothing emits light. No coloured shadows, no halos, no neon edges; a surface separates from its ground by tone and a 1px rule.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour from the `--z-*` tokens so both themes follow; hard-code hexes only inside the dark-in-both-themes result window and capability visuals.",
      "Do keep viridis for data, the colour bar, the brand chip and the progress bar, and the teal accent for links, the current place and focus.",
      "Do render every image from a solved Zephyr case with `docs/scripts/render_loading.py`, keeping its provenance comment, and name the case beside the image.",
      "Do separate surfaces with a 1px cool rule and a tonal step.",
      "Do hold prose, headings, notes and captions to the 42rem measure and let tables, code and figures run wider.",
      "Do keep hover and focus to 150ms colour and border changes, with a 2px accent outline offset 2px for focus.",
      "Do honour reduced motion: the resolve and every transition collapse to nothing."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add glow, coloured shadows, or shadows on code blocks, notes or keys.",
      "Don't introduce a second accent hue or use viridis as decoration away from data.",
      "Don't place an illustration, stock image or mock screenshot; images are the library's output.",
      "Don't let the result window or capability visuals follow the light theme.",
      "Don't set labels, headings or prose in Red Hat Mono.",
      "Don't pin a crate version in prose, install lines or examples."
    ]
  }
}
